# Xana — what belongs in the repository.
#
# This project lives inside a OneDrive folder, so the directory it sits in
# contains a great deal that is not Xana: a 437 MB clone of another project,
# two dependency trees, build output, and the assistant's own runtime state.
# The rules below are the line between "the app" and "everything that happens
# to be next to the app". `git add -A` should never pick up any of it.
#
# The test for anything you are unsure about: would a fresh clone need it, or
# can it be regenerated? If it can be regenerated, it is ignored here.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
# --------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/

# TypeScript. `next-env.d.ts` is generated on every install, and the
# tsbuildinfo is a cache that goes stale the moment a file changes.
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# The npm cache is deliberately kept inside the project (see .npmrc) so that
# installs need no access outside the working directory. That makes it a
# 360 MB directory sitting in the repository root, and it is never committed.
.npm-cache/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Every .env variant, but not the example file: a documented template is how
# someone else knows which variables exist.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Xana's runtime state
# --------------------------------------------------------------------

# The SQLite store and the settings file, which holds API keys in plaintext.
# This is the user's life, not the repository's. It is safe to delete — she
# rebuilds from empty — but it must never be published.
data/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Impeccable skill clone
# --------------------------------------------------------------------

# A full clone of https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable, used as a design
# reference while building the interface. It is a git repository in its own
# right (hence the exclusion rather than a submodule — this is a steerable
# overlay, not a pinned dependency), it is 437 MB, and none of it is ours to
# publish. Nothing in `src/`, `scripts/` or the config references it at
# runtime; `DESIGN.md` is the contract that survived it.
.impeccable/

# The critique reports that came out of that review pass. Kept on disk as the
# record of why the interface looks the way it does, deliberately not
# published. Remove this line to version them.
.impeccable-review/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local agent and editor configuration
# --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Per-machine instructions and permissions for whichever coding tool is in
# use. Useful locally, meaningless to a clone.
.claude/
.dsh/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system
# --------------------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
